## Delivery paths

| Artifact | Path | Wrong (invalid) |
|----------|------|-----------------|
| **Manifest JSON** | **`idea-stage/experiment-plan.manifest.result.json`** | under `refine-logs/` |
| Experiment plan (EN) | **`refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_PLAN.en.md`** | `EXPERIMENT_PLAN.md` only, or wrong folder |
| Experiment plan (ZH) | **`refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_PLAN.zh.md`** | |
| Experiment tracker (EN) | **`refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_TRACKER.en.md`** | `EXPERIMENT_TRACKER.md` only |
| Experiment tracker (ZH) | **`refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_TRACKER.zh.md`** | |

## result

**Delivery only** — not whether the plan is feasible or will succeed.

- `"success"` — valid JSON; non-empty `summary` fields; **all four** deliverable files exist and are non-empty; `EXPERIMENT_PLAN.en.md` contains **all required EN H2 sections**; `EXPERIMENT_PLAN.zh.md` contains **all required ZH H2 sections** (see authoring); both trackers have run table with ≥1 data row; **data access verification** satisfied (URLs, schemas, **schema matches actual data when present**, **experiment blocks aligned with acquisition section**); if `idea-stage/idea-creator.manifest.result.json` exists, `idea_title` matches rank-1 title byte-for-byte.
- `"failed"` — could not complete contract. Still write the manifest file.
- **Do not** use `"partial"` or other values.

## Top-level fields

| Field | Value |
|-------|--------|
| result | `"success"` or `"failed"` |
| aris_phase | `"experiment-plan"` |
| focus_rank | **1** when tied to idea-creator; omit or `null` if no idea manifest |
| idea_title | byte-for-byte rank-1 `ideas[].title` when idea-creator manifest present |
| source_proposal | path string or `null` if derived only from prompt |
| summary | object with `must_run_blocks`, `highest_risk`, `first_runs` (each non-empty for success) |
| finished_at | UTC ISO-8601 |

## deliverables

| Key | Path (exact) | Required for success |
|-----|--------------|----------------------|
| experiment_plan_en | `refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_PLAN.en.md` | yes — non-empty; EN H2s below |
| experiment_plan_zh | `refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_PLAN.zh.md` | yes — non-empty; ZH H2s below |
| experiment_tracker_en | `refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_TRACKER.en.md` | yes — non-empty; run table |
| experiment_tracker_zh | `refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_TRACKER.zh.md` | yes — non-empty; run table |

---

## Authoring: `refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_PLAN.en.md`

**Structure (ARIS `/experiment-plan`):**

After `# Experiment Plan` (or `# Experiment Plan: …`), include metadata (**Problem**, **Method Thesis**, **Date**) then these **H2 sections in order** (each non-empty):

| H2 | Content |
|----|---------|
| `## Claim Map` | Optional one-line note: **C** = claim, **E** = experiment; **C1** primary, **C2** optional. Table: Claim \| Why It Matters \| Minimum Convincing Evidence \| Linked Blocks (E1, E2, …) |
| `## Paper Storyline` | Main paper must prove / appendix / cut |
| `## Experiment Data Acquisition` | … **`### Data download`**: prefer **free direct-download** URLs first; gated/paid links as fallback; each URL **verified** (see **Data access verification**). N/A OK; do not omit H2 |
| `## Experiment Blocks` | Each block: claim, **dataset/split tied to Experiment Data Acquisition** (method 1/2, paths, schema fields), baselines, metrics, success/failure, priority MUST-RUN or NICE-TO-HAVE |
| `## Run Order and Milestones` | Table M0… with decision gates, cost, risk |
| `## Compute and Data Budget` | GPU-hours, data prep, human eval, bottleneck |
| `## Risks and Mitigations` | Table or bullets |
| `## Final Checklist` | `- [ ]` items |

---

## Authoring: `refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_PLAN.zh.md`

Same content as the English plan in **Simplified Chinese**. **Translation rule:** write for researchers **in this field**—use established **专业术语** (methods, metrics, cohorts, clinical/neuro/imaging/ML terms as appropriate). Do not mirror English sentence structure or invent non-standard Chinese for standard concepts. Contract section titles below stay fixed; body text and table cells use field-appropriate Chinese.

Use these **contract H2** (may add English gloss in parentheses, e.g. `## 论点与实验对照（Claim Map）`):

| H2 | Content |
|----|---------|
| `## 论点与实验对照` | 表前可加一句：**C**＝论点；**C1**＝主论点，**C2**＝辅助论点（可选做）。**E**＝实验。表头 **论点**；「对应实验模块」填 E1/E2… |
| `## 论文叙事` | 正文须证明 / 附录 / 可删 |
| `## 实验数据获取` | 同上；**方法二** 下载地址 **优先免费、免申请的直接下载源**，不足再写需注册/申请/购买的备选；URL 须验证可用。详见 **Data access verification** |
| `## 实验模块` | `### 模块 E1：` 等与 EN 一一对应；**数据集/划分须引用上文实验数据获取（方法一/二）的真实路径与结构**，不得另起未定义数据源 |
| `## 运行顺序与里程碑` | 与 EN 里程碑表一致 |
| `## 算力与数据预算` | 与 EN 预算一致 |
| `## 风险与缓解` | 与 EN 风险表一致 |
| `## 终检清单` | `- [ ]` 与 EN checklist 对应 |

Rules (both languages): every block defends a claim; no fabricated results; separate must-run from nice-to-have; **data acquisition section is the single source of truth for what data exists**—blocks and tracker runs must use it.

---

## Data access verification (required for `result: success`)

Planning **must not** copy unchecked URLs or guessed folder trees. Before marking the manifest `"success"`:

### 方法二：数据下载 — URL

- **Source preference (when choosing links to document):** search for **free, direct-download** sources first—open mirrors, official public buckets, Zenodo/Figshare/OpenNeuro-style portals, or documented **anonymous HTTP/FTP** endpoints that do **not** require registration, consortium approval, or purchase. List those as **primary** URLs when they satisfy the study needs (full cohort or an documented subset for M0/sanity). Only if no adequate open path exists, add **secondary** links for apply-to-access / DUA / paid access, and explain why open data is insufficient.
- Every URL in **`#### 下载地址` / `#### Download URLs`** must be **verified in this run** when network/tools allow: e.g. `WebFetch`, `curl -I`, HEAD request, or a **small test download** that proves the link resolves and data can be retrieved (not only a landing page that 404s).
- In the plan, record per link: **验证状态** (e.g. `已验证 YYYY-MM-DD，方式：curl/WebFetch/试下载`) and HTTP/outcome in one line.
- **Forbidden in finished plans:** placeholder URLs, dead links, or “待补” without verification.
- If login/credentials block automated fetch: verify the **official access page** loads, document **未试下载（需账号）**, and do **not** claim “已验证可下载” until a test download succeeded or the user confirms.

### 方法一 / 方法二 — 数据结构（`#### 数据结果` / `#### Data products and layout`）

- The **directory tree, file formats, and table/schema** described must be **validated against a primary source**: official dataset documentation, datacard, README from the provider, or inspection of a **sample file** (subset download, open metadata, or existing project copy).
- In the plan, cite **核对依据** (doc URL, section, or path inspected) and mark **结构已核对** with date.
- **Forbidden:** inventing column names, paths, or formats not confirmed by docs or a real file listing.
- If only the protocol is fixed (方法一, data not yet collected): describe the **planned** schema from the approved protocol/instrument spec and mark **结构已核对（依据：协议/量表文档 …）**—still no invented fields.

### 数据结构须与「真实拿到」一致

- When data **already exists** in the workspace or was obtained via **试下载 / 子集**： the **`#### 数据结果`** description must **match what is actually on disk** (directory listing, opened sample file, metadata row). Reconcile plan text with `ls`, `head`, parquet/schema tools, or provider README—do not keep a doc-only schema that contradicts real files.
- Record **一致性问题** if docs ≠ files; fix the plan or note the delta before `result: success`. **Forbidden:** describing columns/paths that are not present in the material you inspected.

### 实验模块必须基于「实验数据获取」

- **`## Experiment Blocks` / `## 实验模块`** (E1, E2, …) must be **grounded in `## Experiment Data Acquisition` / `## 实验数据获取`** only:
  - Each block’s **dataset / split / task** ( **`数据集 / 划分 / 任务`** ) must name **which method** applies (**方法一：实验获取** and/or **方法二：数据下载**), the **same cohort/slug/paths**, and fields that exist in the documented **数据结果** schema.
  - Do not introduce a **new** external dataset, path, or table layout in E-blocks that was not defined (and verified) in the data-acquisition section.
  - Metrics, covariates, and QC in E-blocks must be **computable from** those files/columns (or from outputs of方法一 if the block is on derived data—state the derivation chain).
- Optional: one short **数据依赖** line per block (e.g. `数据依赖：方法二 → data/rest-meta/…，被试表 subjects.csv 列 …`).

If blocks assume data that the acquisition section does not supply, set manifest **`result: failed`** or revise until aligned.

If verification cannot be completed after reasonable attempts, set manifest **`result: failed`** (do not ship a plan with unverified download URLs or unconfirmed schemas).

---

## Authoring: `refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_TRACKER.en.md` and `EXPERIMENT_TRACKER.zh.md`

**Chinese tracker:** same **专业术语** rule as the Chinese plan; **Run ID / Priority / Status** values match EN (e.g. `MUST`, `TODO` may stay English or use fixed bilingual convention—pick one pair and use consistently in both tracker files).

Follow **`md_template/EXPERIMENT_TRACKER.en.example.md`** and **`md_template/EXPERIMENT_TRACKER.zh.example.md`**: header metadata, **`## Run Execution Table`** (or ZH **`## 运行执行表`**) with columns:

| Run ID | Milestone | Purpose | System / Variant | Split | Metrics | Priority | Status | Notes |

At least one data row (e.g. `R001`, `TODO`). **EN and ZH trackers must share the same Run IDs, Priority, and Status** (Notes may differ by language). Optional sections from the template — milestone gates, compute allocation, data dependencies, risk, manuscript checklist — should mirror between EN and ZH when present.

